# Code

Inline `code`, a padded `` `tick` `` span and a path like `Library/files/2026-11/plan.pdf` in a sentence. A double-backtick span written over three lines, ``npm run
build &&
npm test``, shows on one line.

```ts
// A TypeScript block, highlighted in greys.
export function greet(name: string): string {
  const count = 3;
  return `Hello, ${name}! You have ${count} notes.`;
}
```

```python
def total(rows):
    """Sum the cost column."""
    return sum(row["cost"] for row in rows if row is not None)
```

